  <title>
    <media type="image" width="40px" height="40px" its:translate="no" src="figures/orca-logo.svg" /> Sleep mode
  </title>
  <p>
    Sleep mode temporarily disables Orca for the current application. While Orca is asleep for
    an application, only the command to toggle sleep mode remains available. Use it again to
    wake Orca.
  </p>
  <section id="settings-sleep-mode">
    <title>Settings</title>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Preferences location:</em>
      <gui>Sleep mode</gui> category (global only).
    </p>
    <p>
      Add running applications that should automatically start asleep, then enable or disable
      automatic sleep mode for each application in the list. An application must be running to
      add it; saved applications remain listed even when they are not running.
    </p>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Available settings:</em>
    </p>
    <list>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Always use sleep mode with these applications</gui>: Lists the
          applications for which you can enable automatic sleep mode.
        </p>
      </item>
    </list>
  </section>
  <section id="commands-sleep-mode">
    <title>Commands</title>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Preferences location:</em>
      <gui>Commands</gui> category, <gui>Commands</gui> section, <gui>Sleep mode</gui> group.
    </p>
    <list>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Toggle sleep mode for the current application</gui>
          <keyseq>
            <key>Ctrl</key>
            <key>Alt</key>
            <key>Shift</key>
            <key>Q</key>
          </keyseq>
        </p>
      </item>
    </list>
  </section>
